From 0214996e6bd66abf70af425f0320b18728da5ac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:50:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v2.1.1: backlog bug batch (CGI i18n, rmcpd hardening,
 rwarden perf, 3-page UI align, Lock confirm)

Deferred-backlog items from the 2026-08-02 pre-release review + UI reports:

web.c (do_reaper_dev/gk/warden/mcp CGIs): 37 hardcoded English error
strings now carry a machine key ("ek":"RDEVE_n"/"RADVE_n") alongside the
raw English (kept as fallback). Reaper_Devices/Advisor/Storage map the key
to a dict token -> the alert()/setMsg() errors localize instead of bypassing
the dictionary. Tier-3 i18n gap closed.

rmcpd.c: (1) STRUCTURAL secret-redaction - sb_scrub_secrets() runs at the
single tools/call emit choke point, so every tool (present and future) is
scrubbed, not just get_logs; fail-closed (withhold on OOM). (2) truncation
no longer emits malformed JSON - sb_mark_truncated() marks a cut, and all
three JSON emitters fall back to a small valid envelope when the buffer
hits the cap instead of sending one cut mid-structure.

rwarden.c: threat + geo feed loading (v4/v6, 4 loops) switched from one
`ipset add` fork per CIDR to a single `ipset restore` batch, with the
per-entry loop kept as an automatic fallback on a malformed entry.

www esc() defense-in-depth: Reaper_Conn (flow tuple fields), Reaper_QoSDiag
(port names), Reaper_QoS:492 (class-name input) now wrap system-supplied
strings in the page's escape helper.

UI viewport alignment (shared root cause): Reaper_Conn, Reaper_QoSDiag,
Reaper_WiFiPro used a centered max-width/fit-content wrap (margin:0 auto;
WiFiPro sized off 100vw incl. the shell rail) that shifted them right /
overflowed the iframe vs the full-bleed older pages. All three now fill and
left-align like Reaper_QoS/Traffic. Reaper_Conn also: "Q" flow-table header
-> RCON_35 "QoS Class" (column widened 34->58px, Path 96->84px); page h1
22->26px and flow-detail title 17->20px.

Reaper_Wireless: Channel Lock now shows the same restart/~20s-client-drop
confirmation Unlock got in v1.9.9a (new RWIF_81), before it applies.

Dicts: RDEVE_1-13 + RADVE_1-19 + RCON_35 + RWIF_81 added to all 25 in
lockstep (6155 -> 6189).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
